sequenceDiagram
    participant CLI as CLI Entry Point
    participant Cmd as XRCmd / CompCmd
    participant Loader as CompositeLoader
    participant CDP as DefaultCompDiffProcessor
    participant DP as DefaultDiffProcessor
    participant CompClient as CompositionClient
    participant FnProv as FunctionProvider
    participant Render as Render Function
    participant ReqProv as RequirementsProvider
    participant Resolver as CompositeResolver
    participant ResMgr as ResourceManager
    participant Validator as SchemaValidator
    participant DiffCalc as DiffCalculator
    participant Compare as compare.GenerateDiff
    participant Tree as ResourceTreeClient
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API
    participant Renderer as DiffRenderer / CompDiffRenderer

    CLI->>Cmd: Run()
    Cmd->>Loader: Load()
    Loader-->>Cmd: []*Unstructured

    Note over Cmd, CDP: Outer setup differs by subcommand. The per-XR body is identical.
    alt comp subcommand
        Cmd->>CDP: Initialize(ctx)
        Cmd->>CDP: DiffComposition(ctx, comps, ns, resources)
        CDP->>CompClient: FindComposites(ctx, comp, opts)
        CompClient-->>CDP: [affected XRs]
        Note over CDP, Compare: Composition-level diff, once per composition, up to three local comparisons
        CDP->>Compare: GenerateDiff(ctx, currentComp, newComp, logger, Options)
        Compare-->>CDP: displayed diff (user's --ignore-paths and display masks applied)
        opt Nothing displayed
            CDP->>Compare: GenerateDiff(..., Options{IgnorePaths: nil, ForVerdict: true})
            Compare-->>CDP: did the composition change at all (masks lifted)?
            opt Changed
                CDP->>Compare: GenerateDiff(..., Options{IgnorePaths: [last-applied-configuration], ForVerdict: true})
                Compare-->>CDP: is last-applied-configuration the sole delta (revision name unpredictable)?
            end
        end
        Note over CDP, DP: For each affected XR, CDP calls DP.DiffSingleResource with a provider that returns the proposed composition, and the predicted revision name for a composite that would re-point. See per-XR body below.
    else xr subcommand
        Cmd->>DP: Initialize(ctx)
        Cmd->>DP: PerformDiff(ctx, resources, clusterCompositionProvider)
        Note over DP: PerformDiff iterates the input resources, calling DiffSingleResource on each. See per-XR body below.
    end

    rect rgb(245, 245, 255)
        Note over DP, DiffCalc: per-XR body. DiffSingleResource(ctx, xr, compositionProvider). Driven once per input XR (xr) or once per affected XR (comp).
        loop For each XR being diffed
            DP->>DP: SanitizeXR(res) = authoredXR
            DP->>Resolver: Resolve(ctx, authoredXR, existingNested)
            Resolver->>ResMgr: FetchCurrentObject (the XR unless a nested XR copy is supplied, plus a claim backing XR)
            ResMgr-->>Resolver: cluster copy / backing XR (fetch error is fatal)
            Resolver-->>DP: EffectiveComposite (Authored, Cluster, Backing, Effective)
            Note over DP: Effective = input + cluster's compositionRef / compositionRevisionRef / policy / UID, or a claim's backing XR with the claim synced in. renderXR = strict Defaulter.Default(Effective). authoredXR stays as written: it is the payload.
            DP->>CompClient: compositionProvider(ctx, renderXR)
            CompClient-->>DP: ResolvedComposition (cluster's composition and revision, or proposed under comp)
            Note over DP: If a revision was resolved, set renderXR's compositionRevisionRef to it (creating the ref if absent), as the reconciler does before composing.
            DP->>FnProv: GetFunctionsForComposition(comp)
            FnProv-->>DP: []Function
            DP->>ResMgr: FetchObservedResources(ctx, Composed())
            ResMgr-->>DP: observed composed resources (fetch failure is fatal)
            DP->>DP: RenderToStableState(ctx, renderXR, comp, fns, id, observed, eventualState)
            loop Until requirements stabilise (or steady state under --eventual-state)
                DP->>Render: Render(ctx, inputs)
                Note over Render: Before starting a function for the first time - take this run's lease, reclaim dead runs' containers and networks, then the engine creates a network labelled with this run's session and each container is labelled with it too
                Render-->>DP: CompositionOutputs (incl. RequiredResources)
                alt Has unresolved RequiredResources
                    DP->>ReqProv: ResolveSelectors(ctx, selectors, ns)
                    ReqProv->>K8sAPI: GetResource / GetResourcesByLabel
                    K8sAPI-->>ReqProv: resources
                    ReqProv-->>DP: additional inputs
                end
            end

            DP->>DP: removeNamespacesFromClusterScopedResources(...)
            DP->>Validator: ValidateResources(authoredXR, composed)
            Validator->>Validator: ValidateScopeConstraints for each resource
            Validator-->>DP: ok / err (inputs left unmodified)

            DP->>DiffCalc: CalculateNonRemovalDiffs(ctx, authoredXR, desired)
            loop For each rendered resource
                DiffCalc->>ResMgr: FetchCurrentObject
                ResMgr->>K8sAPI: GET
                K8sAPI-->>ResMgr: current
                alt current != nil
                    DiffCalc->>K8sAPI: DryRunApply(desired, fieldOwner)
                    K8sAPI-->>DiffCalc: result
                else addition, --dry-run-on=all
                    DiffCalc->>K8sAPI: DryRunCreate(desired)
                    K8sAPI-->>DiffCalc: result / Forbidden / Invalid
                    opt Forbidden
                        DiffCalc->>K8sAPI: SelfSubjectAccessReview (memoized)
                        K8sAPI-->>DiffCalc: allowed? => degrade or report
                    end
                else addition, --dry-run-on=existing
                    DiffCalc->>DiffCalc: lenient Defaulter.Default(desired), mark dryRun.skipReason=disabled (+ storageVersion if the CRD stores another version)
                end
                DiffCalc->>Compare: GenerateDiff(ctx, current, wouldBeResult, logger, Options)
                Compare-->>DiffCalc: ResourceDiff
            end
            DiffCalc-->>DP: diffs + rendered (keys, desired resource names per composite)

            opt Nested XRs present
                DP->>DP: ProcessNestedXRs(..., depth+1)
                DP->>DP: Recurse via diffSingleResourceInternal with the nested XR's cluster copy, without removal detection (err if depth > --max-nested-depth)
                Note over DP: Merge the nested diffs and rendered resources into this XR's, so removal detection sees what nested XRs still compose
            end

            opt Top-level XR that exists in the cluster
                DP->>DiffCalc: CalculateRemovedResourceDiffs(ctx, existingXR, rendered)
                DiffCalc->>Tree: GetResourceTree(ctx, existingXR)
                Tree-->>DiffCalc: live resource tree
                Note over DiffCalc: Walk the tree. A composed resource is removed when its composite no longer desires its composition resource name
                DiffCalc->>Compare: GenerateDiff(ctx, removed, nil, logger, Options)
                Compare-->>DiffCalc: removal ResourceDiff
                DiffCalc-->>DP: removal diffs
            end
        end
    end

    Note over CDP, Render: Cleanup runs before output is rendered, so a teardown advisory reaches warnings[]
    alt comp subcommand
        CDP->>DP: Cleanup(ctx)
    end
    DP->>FnProv: Cleanup(ctx)
    DP->>Render: Cleanup(ctx)
    Note over Render: The run removes its labelled containers, the engine removes its network, the run removes any of its networks left, then releases its lease
    alt comp subcommand
        CDP->>Renderer: RenderCompDiff(output)
    else xr subcommand
        DP->>Renderer: RenderDiffs(groups, errs, warnings)
    end

    Renderer-->>Cmd: formatted output
    Cmd-->>CLI: ExitCode
